## P2: ONE READ AT A TIME, AND NEVER MORE THAN THE DOCUMENT (finding 2; by PROPERTY first)
**The property.** (1) A read started while another read of the same stream is in flight is refused with `InvalidOperationException` before it touches any state (D5); the read in flight is not disturbed and ends as it would have. (2) **Separately, and whatever the caller does: the sum of the counts the stream has returned never exceeds the document's total, `Offset` never exceeds it, and no byte is yielded from an answer whose range start is not the offset that was asked for** (D6).
**The review's reproduction (RELAYED; `StreamAttack.cs:283-298`, log row 129):** a body that goes on beyond the range asked (its `Tail = 2`: foreign bytes 0xEE for ever after the 10 document bytes); a first read of 10 held at the first document byte; a second read of 10 started; then the first released. At the head: "no refusal: the second read got 10 bytes, the first 10; the stream yielded 20 bytes for a document of 10; Offset reads 20". Why (DERIVED from `:106`): each read took its cap from the same offset before either finished.
**The class this belongs to.** The review's commission makes "document bytes that are wrong, duplicated or dropped without an error" a Blocker; the review did not grade this row a Blocker because it needs a caller that breaks the one-read rule AND an answer longer than asked. The cells that would have caught each kind at the head:
| Kind | Where the head does it | The cell that is RED on the head |
|---|---|---|
| a WRONG byte (a byte that is not the document's at that offset) | the held first read of the row above receives 10 bytes of the surplus | R01 (its byte assertion); T01 |
| MORE than the total | the same row: 20 for 10 | R01 (its count assertion); R05 for a body that reports more than it was asked for |
| a DUPLICATED byte | two reads that open two answers at one offset (two reads at once with no body yet: DERIVED, not run by anyone) | T01 (the union of yielded positions holds a position twice) |
| a byte DROPPED without an error | not found by the review in 30,000 runs with one read at a time; with two reads at once: DERIVED possible (one read moves the offset while the other's bytes are discarded by a failure) | T01 (a gap in the yielded positions with no exception) |
| bytes handed over AFTER the close | finding 1 | X01 rows 1 to 4, X08 |
**The cells of P2:**
| Cell | What it does | Required | Its red |
|---|---|---|---|
| R01 | the review's row, with your fake: the body that goes on beyond the range; the first read held; a second read started | the second read: `InvalidOperationException`; the first, released, returns bytes that are the document's; the counts returned sum to at most 10; `Offset` at most 10; it prints `READS <second> <first count> <offset>` | RED on the head (20 for 10) |
| R02 | after a refused second read, a THIRD read started while the first is still held | refused too (a refused read releases nothing) | RED on the head; RED under your mutant mG2 |
| R03 | while a read is held: the array overload of `ReadAsync`; `CopyToAsync`; a read into an EMPTY buffer | the first two refused; the empty read returns 0 and touches nothing | RED on the head for the first two |
| R04 | after the held read has ended (with bytes; with an I/O error; with the caller's cancellation: 3 rows) the next read is taken | taken; the bytes are the document's at the offset reached | green on the head; RED under your mutant mG3 (the flag not released on an exception) |
| R05 | a body that REPORTS more bytes than it was asked for: (a) a count above the buffer with a buffer smaller than what remains; (b) a count above what remains | `DocumentFetchException` naming the offset, not retried (1 fetch, 0 waits), the body disposed, `Offset` unchanged | RED on the head (DERIVED: `:113` adds whatever was reported) |
| R06 | a body that reports a NEGATIVE count | treated as a body that ended: a wait and a new fetch at the same offset, as a 0 is (DERIVED from `:111`: say what you see; no change is asked for) | green on the head, it states what is |
| T01 | **several threads at once, which the review did NOT test.** 500 turns (say the number you chose and why); in each: a document of 200 bytes whose byte at offset i is i; a fetch function that answers at once from a script of sound answers, answers cut inside the document (never inside the packet) and failing bodies (every body counts its reads and its disposal, and yields the thread once per read); at a common start signal on pool threads: two readers that read in a loop to the end or to an exception, one closer (alternating the three ways), one canceller of the readers' token. After all four have ended, with NO clock: (1) every exception is one of `ObjectDisposedException`, `InvalidOperationException`, the cancellation exception, an I/O error; (2) each returned buffer holds a run of consecutive values; (3) the values returned to both readers together are exactly 0 to `Offset` minus 1, none twice, none missing; (4) every body ever handed out is disposed; (5) no fetch STARTED after the close had RETURNED | all five in every turn | RED under your mutant mG1 (the refusal removed) in at least one turn: print how many of the 500. **If mG1 leaves all turns green the cell proves nothing: add yield points to the fake or raise the number until it is red, and say so** |
| N01 | every answer gives ONE byte and then fails (the review's row, `StreamAttack.cs:215-217`), total 50 | 50 bytes right, 50 fetches, 49 waits: the name says named limit (D9) | green on the head, it states a limit |

## THE REQUIRED SECTION: WHAT ELSE ARE THE STREAM AND THE READER HANDED THAT IS NOT ONE WELL-BEHAVED CALLER READING ONE WELL-BEHAVED BODY?
(Required. Two lanes of this project lost a round by not asking the second question. "Limit" = named in the XML comment of the type AND in your STATUS, FOR TUESDAY; "out" = not this lane, with where it goes.)
| # | Handed | Did the review test it | After round 2 |
