| 3 | reads, a close and a cancellation from SEVERAL THREADS at once | **NO** (its NOT TESTED list) | **CLOSED for exactly this promise: one read at a time is enforced atomically; a close may come from any thread at any time; nothing else is promised** (T01). `Offset` and `LastPartHeader` read from another thread while a read is in flight may be stale: **Limit** |
| 4 | a close called twice, or by two threads at once, or before any read | twice: yes | **CLOSED**: X07, T01 |
| 5 | a close during the OPEN (the fetch in flight; the packet being read) | no | **CLOSED**: X03, X04; the fetch itself is not cut short: **Limit** (D4) |
| 6 | a close during the wait, or between a failed read and the wait | no | **CLOSED**: X05, X06; the wait itself is not cut short: **Limit** (D4) |
