| 12 | a body or a fetch that throws an exception that is not an I/O error | yes (records 6a): not retried, leaves as it is | unchanged with the stream open; with the stream closed it becomes D1's exception (X09). **FOR RECORDS**, not built |
| 13 | **a REAL HTTP client's body in place of a fake** | **NO** (its NOT TESTED list: finding 1 "rests on two of the four ways a body can end" a held read) | **OUT of this lane** (a test with a real client needs a listener, which this lane may not start): to the transport lane's kit, whose test against its own client must cover a close under a read. **And a Limit, in plain words in the comment: how a real client's body ends a read in flight when it is disposed is not measured; the stream relies on its own look after every await, and on the body ending or failing that read** |
