## Questions with defaults (Tuesday answers at the stamp; every default is already assumed above)
- Q1 (D1, the exception of a read that the close ends): default `ObjectDisposedException`, the ending exception kept inside it. Alternative A: the platform's cancellation exception. Alternative B: an I/O error.
- Q2 (P1, the one clause reached in sense and not in letter): default the count is never reported and the bytes a body wrote during its own disposal are a NAMED limit (cell X08). Alternative: a buffer of the stream's own and a copy on every read, so that no byte reaches a caller's buffer after the close (a copy per read for every document; more code in the last round).
- Q3 (D4, an await in flight at the close): default no signal of the stream's own; a fetch and a wait run to their end, a body that never ends its read is a NAMED limit. Alternative C: a linked cancellation source cancelled by the close.
- Q4 (D5, the refusal of a second read): default `InvalidOperationException`. Alternative D: `NotSupportedException`.
- Q5 (D6, the comparison that only a pair of mutants can prove): default it stays, with that proof said plainly in STATUS and in the READY table. Alternative: only its first half (`read > wanted`), which has a cell of its own; then "never more than the total" rests on the refusal alone.
- Q6 (the required section, row 3, thread-safety): default exactly the three sentences (one read at a time, enforced atomically; a close from any thread; nothing else), proved by T01. Alternative: no promise at all, said in the comment, and a cell that proves the refusal for one thread only (then T01 is not written and D3's order is still built, because the review's own run closes from another thread).
- Q7 (D7, the delimiters 0x06 to 0x0f): default TAKEN and kept with their tag; the standard's text reads that way (THE DELIMITERS). Alternative E: strict, as the head is.
- Q8 (D8, the 80 MiB): default a NAMED limit (the review's files do not show what a legitimate answer needs). Alternative F: a cap on the number of groups, with a number Tuesday names. Alternative G: a bound parameter on the stream.
- Q9 (D9, the retry rule): default as coded, the limit named, cell N01. Alternative H: a ceiling on fetches per document, with a number Tuesday names.
- Q10 (L03, the reader's bound of 0 or below): default the cell is written; if it is RED on the head the guard at `IppReader.cs:26` is fixed in this round. Alternative: the cell only, and a red goes to FOR TUESDAY unfixed.
- Q11 (the review after): default G1 on Fable, round 2 of 2, re-running its own generator, fakes and 37 mutant entries from the folder of READY TABLE at the new head.
- Q12 (the windows and the pane): default READY at Step 0 + 180 minutes, the push by Step 0 + 150, pane `Datasec/OXPd2-X9`.

